  "scope": "Generic organic-support repair, normal Release build/test/link, unchanged-project CLI slicing and application to build/src/Release with live configuration preserved. No commit, push or physical print trial.",
  "causes": [
    "A continuous curved road could pass the old whole-stroke minimum-area check while a long local portion had no underlying material. The screenshot area at Z=23.50 mm contained a 5.58 mm curved cantilever, reaching 2.48 mm from previous support.",
    "A continuation calculated from a nominal plan interval could leave a physical extrusion-height gap at its actual output plane.",
    "Synchronized model-root lookup accepted an extra older model plane after the nearest eligible plane, allowing an additional empty grid layer.",
    "DP/arc path optimization could consume nominal bearing and bridge-curvature margins."
  ],
  "repair": [
    "Check unsupported centerline spans per continuous positive-extrusion entity, rejoining closed-loop seams. A span longer than a line width requires both carried ends and a bounded straight bridge.",
    "Reserve relative path-optimization displacement and area before accepting a foundation. Recheck after simplification using final printed curvature limits.",
    "Continue missing spans toward existing lower support roads within configured organic branch angle, with collision-free physical slabs and valid positive extrusion flow.",
    "Back-propagate bearing using actual adjacent output Z spacing and trim only unlandable offending pieces, preserving adjacent main trunks.",
    "Require the nearest eligible actual printed model foundation at the configured bottom gap, allowing only the documented synchronized-grid quantization.",
    "Use configured line width, layer geometry, branch angle and clearances; no printer-name or input-model-specific code path."
  ],
